                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Jet \colon \mathbf{H}_{/X} \to \mathbf{H}_{/X}
              is (by the discussion there) a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
              on the category of bundles over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOperatorViaJetBundles"}
              says that a differential operators from a bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
              to a bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
              is a morphism from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
              of the jet comonad.
          %p
            Indeed, also the composition of differential operators is the composition in this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
            (e.g.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Marvan93"} Marvan 93, section 1.1
          #CompositionOfDifferentialOperatorsViaCoKleisli.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
