                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde D_1
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Krasilshchik99"} Krasil’shchik 99, theorem 10
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOperatorViaJetBundles"}
            %p
              With this, the morphism that our proposition claims is the correct composite is the total bottom morphism, and the differential operator that this defines by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialOperatorViaJetBundles"}
              is the further composite with the left vertical morphism. Therefore the commutativity of the total diagram gives that this is equal to the total top morphisms, which is the composite of the two differential operators as claimed.
          %p
            The co-Kleisli-like composition for finite order differential operators also appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Kock10"}> Kock 10, section 7.3
            ), from a perspective of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
          %h3#DefinitionInDifferentialCohesion In differential cohesion
          %p
            In view of the
            %a{:href => "#DefinitionInDifferentialGeometry"} above
            one may axiomatize the category of differential operators in any context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+comonad"} jet comonad
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Jet
                    %mi X
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Jet_X \coloneqq i^\ast i_\ast
          %p
            induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi X
