            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spencer+cohomology"} Spencer cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p
            A coordinate-free definition of a linear differential operator suitable for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            in Proposition IV.16.8.8(b) of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Grothendieck"}> A. Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Dieudonn%C3%A9"} J. Dieudonné
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89l%C3%A9ments+de+g%C3%A9om%C3%A9trie+alg%C3%A9brique"} Éléments de géométrie algébrique
                    IV. Étude locale des schémas et des morphismes des schémas, Quatrième partie
            %li#Marvan86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Marvan"}> Michal Marvan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A note on the category of partial differential equations
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential geometry and its applications
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MarvanJetComonad.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p (notice that prop. 1.3 there holds only when the equalizer exists in the first place)
            %li#Saunders89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Saunders"}> David Saunders
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of jet bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 142
            %li#Saito89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morihiko+Saito"}> Morihiko Saito
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Induced D-modules and differential complexes
                %a{:href => "http://smf4.emath.fr/Publications/Bulletin/117/pdf/smf_bull_117_361-387.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Hoermander90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+H%C3%B6rmander"}> Lars Hörmander
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The analysis of linear partial differential operators
            %li#Marvan93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Marvan"}> Michal Marvan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Zero-Curvature Representations of Partial Differential Equations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.45.5631"} web
            %li#KrasilshchikVerbovetsky98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Krasil%27shchik"}> Joseph Krasil'shchik
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Verbovetsky"} Alexander Verbovetsky
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homological Methods in Equations of Mathematical Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9808130"} arXiv:math/9808130
            %li#Krasilshchik99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Krasil%27shchik"} Joseph Krasil'shchik
                in collaboration with Barbara Prinari,
                %em Lectures on Linear Differential Operators over Commutative Algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "https://diffiety.mccme.ru/preprint/99/01_99.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Discussion from a point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Kock10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Synthetic geometry of manfiolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://home.imf.au.dk/kock/SGM-final.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On differential operators in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Jet functors in noncommutative geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00029-025-01064-3"} doi.org/10.1007/s00029-025-01064-3
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
                %em Symbols in noncommutative geometry
                (2023). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.00835"}> arXiv:2308.00835
                )
            %li
              %p
                Keegan J. Flood, Mauro Mantegazza, Henrik Winther.
